# UniFi Connect / wall-panel APK versioning

UniFi Connect rejects APK uploads with "Outdated App File" unless `versionCode` is **strictly higher** than the installed app. The entrance tablet uses the same bump so admin-page sideload also requires a newer `versionCode`.

## When building or handing over an APK

- After any change meant for a wall tablet, run `./gradlew :app:assembleGreatroomDebug` or `./gradlew :app:assembleEntranceDebug` (or `assembleRelease` / `packageDebug` / `packageRelease`). Those tasks auto-bump `versionCode` and `versionName` in `app/version.properties`.
- Never tell the user to upload an existing APK without rebuilding first.
- Never reuse a previously built APK. Rebuild even if sources look unchanged — a second assemble produces a higher `versionCode`.
- Do not bump by hand-editing `defaultConfig` in `app/build.gradle.kts`. Do not bump on Gradle sync or compile-only tasks.
- Do not auto-commit `app/version.properties` (a dirty tree after assemble is expected).

```bash
# ❌ BAD — reuse last APK
# "Upload app/build/outputs/apk/greatroom/debug/ha-native-greatroom-debug.apk"

# ✅ GOOD — rebuild so versionCode increases
./gradlew :app:assembleGreatroomDebug
# then upload app/build/outputs/apk/greatroom/debug/ha-native-greatroom-debug.apk
# Entrance: ./gradlew :app:assembleEntranceDebug
#   → app/build/outputs/apk/entrance/debug/ha-native-entrance-debug.apk
```
